    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0053",
      "reading_order": 57,
      "section": "2.2.3 Bypass Mode",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 77.904,
        "t": 503.1176629101563,
        "r": 541.61568,
        "b": 431.24610136319495
      },
      "content": "Under inverter supply mode, if there is some fault for inverter or overload time of inverter is overdue or switch manually to bypass, the static switch will convert the load from inverter supply to static bypass power supply and the power supply of load is not interrupted. If the inverter and bypass is not synchronous at that time, UPS will switch off the inverter static switch firstly, and then switch on the bypass static switch, and the power supply of load is not interrupted."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0004",
      "reading_order": 58,
      "section": "2.2.3 Bypass Mode",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 78.12254501005964,
        "t": 424.60887561776093,
        "r": 99.24753270287286,
        "b": 405.08741553116704
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0004.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_0053",
      "next_block_id": "txt_0054"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0054",
      "reading_order": 59,
      "section": "2.2.3 Bypass Mode",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 77.904,
        "t": 412.1576629101563,
        "r": 541.2132799999995,
        "b": 384.42610136319496
      },
      "content": "Note:  When  UPS  is  under  bypass  mode,  load  cannot  be  protected  by  UPS  if  voltage  or frequency changes or power is down."
    },
